            <ArticleTitle>Toward a profile of medically ill psychiatric patients.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>822-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We reviewed 564 consecutive psychiatric inpatient admissions. In support of previous studies, we found 51.9% to have significant medical disorders, nearly half of them &quot;new&quot; or previously unsuspected. Women, the elderly, substance abusers, and patients with nonschizophrenic functional psychoses had a higher prevalence of medical disorders. Using this information as a starting point, further work should be done to define a profile of the psychiatric patients at highest risk for medical illnesses.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
